// Package sce provides the runtime support library for W3C SCXML 1.0 state
// machines generated by sce-codegen generate -l go. This package provides:
//
//   - StatePolicy: the interface contract that generated state machine code implements
//   - Engine: the execution engine parameterized on a StatePolicy via Go generics
//   - EventMetadata, EventWithMetadata: §scxml-5.10 event wrappers
//   - HttpSendRequest: §scxml-C-2 BasicHTTP event processor support
//   - The W3C SCXML Appendix D microstep: selection, conflict removal, exit
//     and entry sets, history, completion (microstep.go)
//   - Event descriptor matching (§scxml-3.12.1)
//   - PullScheduler: delayed event scheduling (§scxml-6.2)
//
// This package is a 1:1 port of the Rust runtime at sce-rust-runtime/. Method
// names, field layouts, and semantics match the Rust (and C++) source. When the
// Rust and Go versions diverge, Rust wins.
//
// # Threading
//
// The rule is ARCHITECTURE.md "Engine Threading" (docs/adr/0084). An Engine
// belongs to the goroutine that drives it, and Engine's own documentation names
// its owner-goroutine operations. Another goroutine reaches it through
// Engine.Inbox, the one handle that is safe for concurrent use; a host does not
// put a lock of its own around an engine.
//
// # Generics
//
// The Engine and StatePolicy use Go type parameters (generics) with the
// comparable constraint for State and Event types. Generated code produces
// concrete types satisfying StatePolicy[S, E].
package sce
